<div class="bubble-measurements" aria-label="Bubble mailer outer and usable inner size illustrations">
  <figure>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 320 285" role="img" aria-label="Flat bubble mailer showing outer width, body length and a separate closure flap">
      <rect x="65" y="55" width="170" height="190" rx="7" fill="#fff" stroke="#203c30" stroke-width="2" />
      <path d="M65 92H235" stroke="#b63b10" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />
      <path d="M65 30H235M65 23V37M235 23V37M260 92V245M253 92H267M253 245H267" fill="none" stroke="#203c30" stroke-width="2" />
      <text x="150" y="20" text-anchor="middle">Outer width</text>
      <text x="150" y="80" text-anchor="middle" class="flap-label">Flap</text>
      <text x="150" y="160" text-anchor="middle">Body</text><text x="150" y="184" text-anchor="middle">length</text>
      <text x="150" y="272" text-anchor="middle">Outer size ≠ inner size</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption><strong>1. Catalogue outer size</strong><span>Outer width × body length + flap. The flap closes the bag; it is listed separately from the body.</span></figcaption>
  </figure>
  <figure>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 320 285" role="img" aria-label="Bubble mailer with a smaller dashed inner area between the side seams and below the flap">
      <rect x="65" y="55" width="170" height="190" rx="7" fill="#fff" stroke="#203c30" stroke-width="2" />
      <path d="M65 92H235" stroke="#203c30" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />
      <rect x="82" y="110" width="136" height="117" rx="5" fill="#f1f3ec" stroke="#b63b10" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />
      <text x="150" y="20" text-anchor="middle">Check the actual sample</text>
      <text x="150" y="157" text-anchor="middle">Usable inner</text><text x="150" y="181" text-anchor="middle">space</text>
      <text x="150" y="272" text-anchor="middle">Lining + seams affect fit</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption><strong>2. Usable inner space</strong><span>Confirm the opening and inner dimensions on the selected sample, then insert and seal your complete packed item.</span></figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>
<p class="bubble-measurement-note">Measurement illustrations only, not to scale. There is no universal amount to subtract for the liner or seams. Packed thickness and closure still need a physical fit check.</p>
<style>
  .bubble-measurements{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px;margin:26px 0 12px}.bubble-measurements figure{margin:0;min-width:0;padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;background:var(--white)}.bubble-measurements svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:360px;margin-inline:auto}.bubble-measurements text{font:18px Inter,Arial,sans-serif;fill:var(--ink)}.bubble-measurements .flap-label{fill:var(--orange)}.bubble-measurements figcaption{font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.65}.bubble-measurements figcaption strong,.bubble-measurements figcaption span{display:block}.bubble-measurements figcaption strong{margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--ink)}.bubble-measurement-note{font-size:.875rem!important;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65}
  @media(max-width:640px){.bubble-measurements{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}.bubble-measurements figure{padding:18px}.bubble-measurements svg{max-width:300px}}
</style>
